<h1><%= h(@community.name) %>: webhooks</h1>

<div class="card muted">
  Where this community's events are sent, and what happened to every attempt at sending one.
  Each delivery is signed, so a subscriber can tell it really came from here; the signature and the
  <code>webhook-id</code>, <code>webhook-timestamp</code> and <code>webhook-signature</code> headers
  follow the Standard Webhooks conventions, so an off-the-shelf library on their side verifies it.
  Delivery is at least once and a subscriber should ignore an id they have already seen.
  Events reach one subscriber in the order they happened: a delivery that has not landed yet holds
  the ones behind it until it lands or is given up on.
  A subscription is created over the REST API rather than here, because creating one hands out a
  signing secret.
  Deliveries are kept for <%= Rubotty::ControlPlane::Webhooks::RETENTION / (24 * 60 * 60) %> days.
</div>

<h2>Subscriptions</h2>
<%= webhook_subscriptions_table(@subscriptions,
                                empty: "Nothing in this community is subscribed to anything.") %>

<h2>Deliveries</h2>
<% if @failed.positive? %>
  <p class="muted">
    <%= @failed %> <%= @failed == 1 ? "delivery has" : "deliveries have" %> been given up on.
    Sending one again puts it back on the queue with its attempts reset, which is what an endpoint
    that has since been fixed needs.
  </p>
<% end %>

<%= webhook_deliveries_table(@deliveries, community: @community,
                             empty: "Nothing has been sent yet.") %>
